module wyd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6-wyoming }

// The District of Wyoming's own civil periods, computed under the federal
// rules (U.S.D.C.L.R. 6.1(a): time limits imposed by the Local Rules are
// computed in accordance with the applicable Federal Rules of Civil
// Procedure). Periods the rules state in business days stay in notes, as
// FRCP 6(a) counts every day: amended pleadings are filed within 3
// business days from entry of the order granting the motion to amend
// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 15.1), the written discovery plan is submitted 3 business
// days before the initial pretrial conference (U.S.D.C.L.R. 16.1(a)(2)),
// and parties notify chambers of an ADR settlement within 3 business days
// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 16.3). Supplemental motion documents may not be filed less
// than 3 working days before a hearing (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(c)(4)), and an
// unpaid filing fee is due within 3 calendar days (U.S.D.C.L.R. 5.1(a)).
// A motion to extend the time to answer or move to dismiss may be granted
// for not more than 14 days (U.S.D.C.L.R. 6.1(b)); that bounds an order,
// not a filing, and stays a note. Periods that restate a federal period
// are lit/frcp's and stay in notes: an objection to a magistrate judge's
// non-dispositive order is sought within 14 days after service of the
// order (U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(a); FRCP 72(a)), and an objection to proposed
// findings and recommendations within 14 days after service
// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(b); FRCP 72(b)(2)). Reply briefs are not filed on a
// motion set for hearing (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D), (b)(2)(C)); the reply
// periods below apply to a motion decided without a hearing. The dispositive
// briefing periods and limits also govern preliminary injunction motions
// and amicus briefs filed with leave (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2), (b)(2)(G)).
// The earlier D. Wyo. outline's FRCP flow and its decisions (Twombly,
// Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Matsushita, Unitherm, Bowles
// v. Russell, Hamer, Microsoft Corp. v. Baker and the Tenth Circuit's
// Robbins v. Oklahoma) are FRCP and FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp
// and lit/frap; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A brief in support of or in opposition to a non-dispositive motion: at
/// most 10 pages (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(C)). A request for
/// reconsideration of a magistrate judge's non-dispositive order, and its
/// response, are subject to the same limit (U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(a)).
limit nondispositive-brief {
  pages <= 10 cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(C)"
} cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(C)"

/// A reply brief on a non-dispositive motion: at most 5 pages
/// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D)).
limit nondispositive-reply {
  pages <= 5 cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D)"
} cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D)"

/// A brief in support of or in opposition to a dispositive motion: at
/// most 25 pages (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(B)). Objections to a magistrate
/// judge's proposed findings and recommendations, and the response, are
/// subject to the same limit (U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(b)).
limit dispositive-brief {
  pages <= 25 cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(B)"
} cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(B)"

/// A reply brief on a dispositive motion: at most 10 pages (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(2)(C)).
limit dispositive-reply {
  pages <= 10 cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(C)"
} cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(C)"

/// Service of the summons and complaint is effected, or the waiver is
/// returned (U.S.D.C.L.R. 4.1(b)).
event ServiceEffected()
/// A non-dispositive motion is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(B)).
event NondispositiveMotionFiled() paper nondispositive-brief
/// The response to a non-dispositive motion is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(1)(B)).
event NondispositiveResponseFiled() paper nondispositive-brief
/// The reply brief on a non-dispositive motion is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(1)(D)).
event NondispositiveReplyFiled() paper nondispositive-reply
/// A dispositive motion and its brief are filed (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(2)(A)).
event DispositiveMotionFiled() paper dispositive-brief
/// The opposing brief on a dispositive motion is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(2)(A)).
event DispositiveResponseFiled() paper dispositive-brief
/// The reply brief on a dispositive motion is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 7.1(b)(2)(C)).
event DispositiveReplyFiled() paper dispositive-reply
/// A deposition is scheduled to be taken under FRCP 30(b)(1)
/// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 30.1(a), 37.1(d)).
event DepositionScheduled()
/// The presiding judge's chambers or the Clerk of Court is notified that
/// the action has settled (U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(a)).
event SettlementNoticed()
/// The Clerk of Court notifies counsel or pro se parties that the case
/// may be dismissed for lack of prosecution (U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(b)).
event ProsecutionNoticeGiven()
/// A final judgment for which costs are allowed is entered (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 54.2(a), 54.3(c)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// The bill of costs is served (U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(b)).
event BillOfCostsServed()
/// The court of appeals issues its mandate (U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(i)).
event MandateIssued()
/// The claim for attorney's fees is filed (U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.3(d)).
event FeeClaimFiled()
/// In a civil case fully assigned to a magistrate judge, a party files an
/// answer or other responsive filing (U.S.D.C.L.R. 73.1).
event ResponsiveFilingInAssignedCase()
/// A request for reconsideration of a magistrate judge's non-dispositive
/// order is served (U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(a)).
event ReconsiderationRequestServed() paper nondispositive-brief
/// The Clerk of this Court enters the Order on Removal (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 81.1).
event RemovalOrderEntered()
/// The court accepts for filing a complaint signed only by an attorney
/// not admitted to this Court (U.S.D.C.L.R. 84.2(b)).
event ComplaintFiledByNonadmittedAttorney()
/// In a proceeding to review agency action, the complaint or petition for
/// review is properly served (U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(2)).
event AgencyPetitionServed()
/// The agency files the administrative record (U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(3),
/// (c)).
event AgencyRecordFiled()
/// The opening brief seeking review of agency action is served
/// (U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c)).
event AgencyOpeningBriefServed()
/// The responsive brief in an agency review is served (U.S.D.C.L.R.
/// 83.6(c)).
event AgencyResponseBriefServed()

/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 4.1(b): proof of service, or waiver of service, of a
/// summons and complaint is filed within 10 days after it is effected or
/// returned, and in any event no later than the time within which the
/// party served must respond.
deadline return-of-service-period: 10.days after ServiceEffected() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 4.1(b)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(B): each party opposing a non-dispositive
/// motion has 14 days after its filing to file a written response; the
/// Court may treat a failure to respond timely as a confession of the
/// motion.
deadline nondispositive-response-period: 14.days after NondispositiveMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(B)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D): for a non-dispositive motion decided
/// without a hearing, a reply brief may be filed within 7 days of the
/// filing of the response brief.
deadline nondispositive-reply-period: 7.days after NondispositiveResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(1)(D)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(A): each party opposing a dispositive motion
/// has 14 days from its filing to file a written brief in opposition; a
/// party that does not intend to oppose a motion not marked unopposed
/// files a notice of non-opposition no later than the same deadline.
deadline dispositive-response-period: 14.days after DispositiveMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(A)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(C): for a dispositive motion decided without a
/// hearing, a reply brief may be filed within 7 days of the filing of the
/// response brief.
deadline dispositive-reply-period: 7.days after DispositiveResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 7.1(b)(2)(C)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 30.1(a): unless the Court orders otherwise, reasonable
/// notice of a deposition under FRCP 30(b)(1) is not less than 14 days,
/// computed under FRCP 6.
deadline deposition-notice-period: 14.days before DepositionScheduled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 30.1(a)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 37.1(d): a motion under FRCP 26(c) directed to a
/// deposition is filed and served as soon as practicable after receipt of
/// the notice, and in no event less than 5 days before the scheduled
/// deposition.
deadline deposition-protective-motion-period: 5.days before DepositionScheduled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 37.1(d)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(a): on notice that an action has settled, counsel
/// file within 30 days, unless otherwise permitted or directed, the
/// filings necessary to terminate it; otherwise the Court may set the
/// action for trial.
deadline settlement-papers-period: 30.days after SettlementNoticed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(a)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(b): after 90 days without action, the Clerk notifies
/// the parties that the case may be dismissed for lack of prosecution 30
/// days from the date of the notice; if no action is taken within 30 days
/// after notice, the Court may enter the order of dismissal.
deadline prosecution-notice-period: 30.days after ProsecutionNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 41.1(b)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(a): within 14 days from entry of a final judgment
/// for which costs are allowed, the prevailing party files a bill of
/// costs (other than attorney's fees) on AO form 133.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(a)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(b): if no objections are filed within 14 days after
/// service of the bill of costs, the Clerk taxes the costs properly
/// claimed.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsServed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(b)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(i): costs taxable under FRAP 39(e) are waived unless
/// the party entitled to them files a bill of costs within 14 days of the
/// issuance of the court of appeals' mandate.
deadline appeal-costs-period: 14.days after MandateIssued() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.2(i)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.3(c), (e): if the parties cannot agree, the moving
/// party files the statement of consultation with a motion for attorney's
/// fees within 14 days of entry of the final judgment; failure to file
/// timely is a waiver unless the Court grants relief for good cause.
deadline fee-motion-period: 14.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.3(c)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.3(d), (e): the opposing party files objections to the
/// fee request within 14 days after the filing of the claim for
/// attorney's fees.
deadline fee-objection-period: 14.days after FeeClaimFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 54.3(d)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 73.1: in a civil case fully assigned to a magistrate
/// judge, each party sends the Clerk's Office, within 14 days from the
/// filing of an answer or other responsive filing, either a written
/// consent under 28 U.S.C. § 636(c) or a written election to have the
/// action reassigned to a district judge.
deadline magistrate-consent-period: 14.days after ResponsiveFilingInAssignedCase() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 73.1"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(a): a response to a request for reconsideration of
/// a magistrate judge's non-dispositive order is filed within 14 days
/// after service of the request.
deadline reconsideration-response-period: 14.days after ReconsiderationRequestServed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 74.1(a)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 81.1: within 14 days of entry of the Order on Removal,
/// the removing party files a copy of the entire state court record and
/// proceedings, including the docket sheet.
deadline removal-record-period: 14.days after RemovalOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 81.1"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 84.2(b): a complaint accepted for filing signed only by
/// an attorney not admitted to this Court is conditioned on association
/// with local counsel within 14 days after the filing of the complaint.
deadline local-counsel-period: 14.days after ComplaintFiledByNonadmittedAttorney() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 84.2(b)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(2): unless a statute provides a different time or
/// the Court orders otherwise, the agency files the record within 90 days
/// of proper service of the complaint or petition for review (60 days in
/// a Social Security case, not encoded separately).
deadline agency-record-period: 90.days after AgencyPetitionServed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(2)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(3): a request for completion of the record, or
/// for consideration of extra-record evidence, is filed within 14 days
/// after the record was filed.
deadline agency-record-supplement-period: 14.days after AgencyRecordFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(b)(3)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c): unless otherwise ordered, the party seeking
/// review serves and files an opening brief within 45 days after the
/// record is filed (after a supplemental record is filed or the motion is
/// denied, if a (b)(3) motion is filed).
deadline agency-opening-brief-period: 45.days after AgencyRecordFiled() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c): the responding party serves and files a brief
/// within 30 days after service of the opening brief.
deadline agency-response-brief-period: 30.days after AgencyOpeningBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c)"
/// U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c): the plaintiff or petitioner may serve and file
/// a reply brief within 14 days after service of the responsive brief.
deadline agency-reply-brief-period: 14.days after AgencyResponseBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-wyoming cite "U.S.D.C.L.R. 83.6(c)"
